## The Sun spin's gains of the flight software, transcribed from adcs-sim config.rs (spin_params): He et al. (2023)'s L1/L2
## Sun-spin gains k1 = 0.01 g and k2 = 0.05 g, and de Ruiter (2011)'s overall gain k = 0.01 g and nutation weight
## k2 = 0.5 J_zz (k2 in inertia units here: the paper's 0.5 times J_zz [kg m^2]), g the scenario's gain scale
## (fsw_tune_ss_gain when it states none). Plain numbers in SI.
## The developer's transcription (S7.13), unsigned.
module fswspin

## The Sun spin's gains from the gain scale g and the inertia about the spin axis jzz [kg m^2].
fn fsw_sun_spin_gains(g: real[1] in 0.1 .. 10, jzz: real[1] in 0.001 .. 1) -> (k1: real[1], k2: real[1], dr_k: real[1], dr_k2: real[1])
    k1 = 0.01*g
    k2 = 0.05*g
    dr_k = 0.01*g
    dr_k2 = 0.5*jzz
end
